From d1b1f0abad2b802253ecd4c385ec3ec19745c31b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:58:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] emacs: pipelined client and a file handler that never
 asks twice

- scrutiny-agent-send/-await: requests are futures; everything a
  command is known to need goes out before the first reply is awaited
- a complete listing proves absence; watched listings never expire
  (fs.changed); find-file is one round trip, completion/dired/stat in
  a directory already seen are none
- save is one conditional write; the first keystroke no longer opens a
  TRAMP session (lock-file et al. are served); missing files signal
  file-missing; remote ~ resolves remotely; user@host names match
- process-file / start-file-process / make-process handler seam
- every hand-off to TRAMP is counted (scrutiny-agent-fs-delegations)
- the agent is started with a --config path the remote shell can
  expand (it was quoted, so ~ never expanded and the agent silently
  came up unconfigured: read-only, no git.exec, rooted at HOME)
- warn at connect when the agent did not load the config it was sent
- deflate negotiation

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019jbckAQJKVB7rWtCNuRt23
